'''Serenno City''' was a [[city]] located in a valley near [[Castle Serenno]], the headquarters of [[House Serenno]], during the reign of [[Dooku]], a former [[Jedi]] turned [[Sith Lord]], as [[Count of Serenno]], below the cliff that the palace was situated upon and opposite the [[eastern ridge]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Serenno]]. The city was close to the [[upper forest region]] of the planet and beyond a [[forest]]. After the end of the [[Clone Wars]], the city was [[Bombardment of Serenno|destroyed]] by the [[Galactic Empire]] via an [[orbital bombardment]]. In [[19 BBY]], [[Hunter]] and [[Wrecker]] who were members of [[Clone Force 99]] attempted to use the city ruins to evade [[Wilco's company]] led by [[Clone Captain]] [[Wilco]].

==History==
{{Quote|Our way out is down.''"<br />"''I knew you were gonna say that.''"<br />"''We use the city ruins for cover and trek back to the Marauder.|Hunter and Wrecker discussing a plan to escape Castle Serenno.|<ref name="Ruins of War">{{TBB|Ruins of War}}</ref>}}
When the [[Clone Wars]] erupted between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], Dooku funded his war effort by not only exploiting other worlds but also stealing from his own people which included the inhabitants of the city.<ref name="Ruins of War" /> After Dooku's [[death]], shortly before the end of the Clone Wars, the [[Galactic Empire]] formed out of the Republic<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref> conquered and [[Occupation of Serenno|occupied]] Serenno. The city was [[Bombardment of Serenno|destroyed]] by [[orbital bombardment]],<ref name="Spoils of War" /> leading to surviving [[Serennian]]s such as [[Romar Adell]] to take up life in hiding in places like Serenno's [[upper forest region]].<ref name="Ruins of War" />

[[File:Ruins_of_war.png|thumb|left|300px|Wrecker and Hunter in the ruins of the city]]
Some [[time]] after the city's destruction, the members of the renegade [[clone commando]] unit [[Clone Force 99]] attempted to [[Mission to Castle Serenno|steal]] some of [[Dooku's war chest]] while [[Imperial Military|Imperial forces]] were preparing to ship it offworld. When things started to go wrong, the [[squad]] was split up<ref name="Spoils of War" /> and the team's leader, [[Hunter]], and his teammate [[Wrecker]] escaped into the ruins of the city while attempting to avoid [[Clone Captain]] [[Wilco]] and his [[Wilco's company|company]] of [[clone trooper]]s.<ref name="Ruins of War" />

Wilco led a pursuit into the city and gained a visual on the two renegade [[Cloning|clones]] while attempting to surround them. Wrecker, however, improvised a cannon out of a destroyed Separatist [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|tank]] which he used to blast a path through the Imperial forces. Hunter and Wrecker escaped the ruins of the city and returned to their [[starship]], the [[Marauder (Omicron-class)|''Marauder'']], to pick up the other members of the team before departing the planet.<ref name="Ruins of War" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:SerennoCity-LightingConcept.png|thumb|right|320px|The lighting concept of Serenno City was done by Molly Denmark.]]
The city first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' [[The Clone Wars: Season Three|third-season]] episode "[[Nightsisters (episode)|Nightsisters]],"<ref name="Nightsisters" /> although it was first explored as a location in the ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'' [[The Bad Batch Season 2|second-season]] episodes "[[Spoils of War]]"<ref name="Spoils of War" /> and "[[Ruins of War]]."<ref name="Ruins of War" /> The exterior of the city lighting concept was done by [[Molly Denmark]] who also did the lighting concept of an [[Alpha-3 Nimbus-class V-wing starfighter|Alpha-3 ''Nimbus''-class V-wing starfighter]] flying over the city.<ref name="Concept Art">{{SW|url=ruins-of-war-concept-art-gallery|text="Ruins of War" Concept Art Gallery &#124; The Bad Batch}} {{C|Slide 6}}</ref>

